        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/0ef8d677-f432-499f-8b1a-c77f14e1c6bb,1771462924615/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1920%2C1080%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Late Show host Stephen Colbert.' width='620' height='349' title='Late Show host Stephen Colbert.'/><p>Late Show host Stephen Colbert is accusing CBS of forbidding him to air his interview with James Talarico \u2014 a Democratic U.S. Senate candidate \u2014 citing Federal Communications Commission (FCC) rules about ensuring a level playing field during elections. Andrew Chang breaks down Colbert's comments about the regulations, explains how they actually work, and puts it all in context with President Donald Trump's ongoing fight against late-night TV.\n\nImages provided by The Canadian Press, Reuters and Getty Images</p>",
